AB  - Explainably estimating confidence in published scholarly work offers o
pportunity for faster and more robust scientific progress. We develop 
a synthetic prediction market to assess the credibility of published c
laims in the social and behavioral sciences literature. We demonstrate
 our system and detail our findings using a collection of known replic
ation projects. We suggest that this work lays the foundation for a re
search agenda that creatively uses AI for peer review.
