AB  - In the past, several works have investigated ways for combining quanti
tative and qualitative methods in research assessment exercises. In th
is work, we aim at introducing a methodology to explore whether citati
on-based metrics, calculated only considering open bibliographic and c
itation data, can yield insights on how human peer-review of research 
assessment exercises is conducted. To understand if and what metrics p
rovide relevant information, we propose to use a series of machine lea
rning models to replicate the decisions of the committees of the resea
rch assessment exercises.
